<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Palanan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Palanan is a remote municipality on the Pacific coast of Isabela province in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luzon">Luzon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>, cut off from the interior by the Sierra Madre mountains. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Emilio Aguinaldo</a>, president of the First Philippine Republic, hid there during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war">Philippine–American War</a> until he was captured on 23 March 1901 by an American force under Frederick Funston, which had entered disguised as prisoners of Macabebe scouts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/palanan.jpg" alt="Palanan" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Staff Sgt. Chad L. Simon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buildings_and_roads_in_the_Philippine_town_of_Palanan_are_visible_from_a_P-3C_Orion_aircraft_carrying_U.S._Sailors_Oct._22,_2010_101022-M-ZA787-148.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
